        "tests": "Store, API and UI tests cover UTC boundaries, leap years, atomic PATCH, filter values, stale responses and failure paths; the one existing test was only updated for the new fields.",
        "conventions": "The change uses ValidationError mapped to 400, adds data-testid on new elements, has no new dependencies and follows the repo's test style.",
        "architecture": "Date logic lives in the store, with a thin HTTP layer and an injectable clock, but the UI tests run the inline script through a hand-rolled vm DOM double.",
        "codeQuality": "Validation is atomic and the clock is read once per list, but the validator has a redundant length check, and fetching `/todos?overdue=false` is never needed."
